course: dictionary
lesson: 1003
title: Bolivia, a country high in the Andes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bolivia is a country in the middle of South America. It has no coast, so it has no sea shore and no beaches on the ocean. Its land is high up in the Andes Mountains, so many of its places are far above sea level.
explain: Read this sentence: «Bolivia is named after Simón Bolívar; its official capital is Sucre, while its government sits in La Paz.» The clues tell you that a country can have one official capital while its government works from another city.
explain: Context also helps with place names. «Silver from Potosí, in today's Bolivia, flowed to Spain from the 1500s.» The words "today's Bolivia" tell you that Potosí is in Bolivia now, and that Bolivia is a country in the present day. Look for these small clues whenever you meet a place name.
fact: Bolivia is a country in South America with no coast.
fact: Bolivia lies high in the Andes Mountains.
fact: Lake Titicaca is shared by Bolivia and Peru.
fact: La Paz is one of the highest capital cities in the world, and it is where Bolivia's government sits.
fact: Bolivia is named after Simón Bolívar, and people there speak Spanish, Quechua and Aymara.
exercise: «Bolivia has no coast.» What does "no coast" mean? | It has no rivers | *It has no sea shore | It has no mountains | It has no cities
exercise: «The Spanish forced Indigenous people to mine the silver mountain of Potosí in Bolivia.» Where was Potosí? | In China | In Peru | *In Bolivia | In Spain
exercise: «Bolivia is named after Simón Bolívar; its official capital is Sucre, while its government sits in La Paz.» Which city is the official capital? | *Sucre | La Paz | Potosí | Lima
test: Which lake does Bolivia share with Peru? | Lake Superior | Lake Como | *Lake Titicaca | Lake Victoria
test: «Silver from Potosí, in today's Bolivia, flowed to Spain from the 1500s; much of the silver ended up in China.» Where did much of the silver end up? | In Bolivia | *In China | In Brazil | In Spain
exam: Which statement about Bolivia is true? | It is an island in the Caribbean | It is in Africa | It has a coast on the Pacific Ocean | *It has no coast and lies high in the Andes
